From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: bcm-pdc: return messages that end in a receive error

For SPU-M, pdc_receive_one() checks the receive status that the DMA
engine writes in front of each response. On an overflow or a zero length
it returns -EIO. By then it has already reclaimed the message's
descriptors and unmapped its buffers, but it never frees the status
buffer or passes the message back to the client. The request that sent
the message never completes, and its caller waits forever.
pdc_receive() also stops at the error, so responses behind it wait for
the next interrupt.

Free the status buffer and return the message with mssg.error set to
-EIO. Set mssg.error to 0 for a good response: mssg is on the stack and
its error field is not initialized.

Fixes: a24532f8d17b ("mailbox: Add Broadcom PDC mailbox driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mailbox/bcm-pdc-mailbox.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/mailbox/bcm-pdc-mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/bcm-pdc-mailbox.c
@@ -633,6 +633,7 @@ pdc_receive_one(struct pdc_state *pdcs)
 		pdcs->pdc_idx, pdcs->txin, pdcs->txout, pdcs->rxin,
 		pdcs->rxout, pdcs->last_rx_curr);
 
+	mssg.error = 0;
 	if (pdcs->pdc_resp_hdr_len == PDC_SPUM_RESP_HDR_LEN) {
 		/*
 		 * For SPU-M, get length of response msg and rx overflow status.
@@ -649,7 +650,7 @@ pdc_receive_one(struct pdc_state *pdcs)
 			} else {
 				dev_info_ratelimited(dev, "crypto rx len = 0");
 			}
-			return -EIO;
+			mssg.error = -EIO;
 		}
 	}
 
